    "category": "feature",
    "source": "Bad Eden (2024 rules)",
    "tags": [],
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>“By morning the trough is dry, the dog is quiet, and the rumor has a new chapter.”</em></p><p><strong>Dry Well (tier uses / Soma Break).</strong> Your bite takes more than blood now. When you hit a creature with Blood-Drinker, you can also drain it: the target can't regain Integrity until the start of your next turn, and you learn one true thing it is afraid of (the GM tells you). A creature drained this way makes its next Soul defense check before the end of your next turn with 3d10 keep lowest 2.</p><p><strong>Thirst Sense.</strong> You always know the direction of the nearest living creature with blood in it within 60 squares, and whether it is wounded.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
